   "date": "2015-10-14T21:02:32Z",
   "subject": "Re: Problem with a ideal point estimation model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Guilherme,</font></span><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\">I&#39;m not familiar with this model in particular (how big is the data?), but one thing to try is vectorizing the call to bernoulli. If you want to use probit then this would entail defining a local variable (an N-vector) in the model block, looping from 1 to N</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Phi_approx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(...);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bernoulli</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># outside the loop</span></div></code></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\">Even better would be to do it on the logit rather than probit scale because we have a vectorized bernoulli_logit function which is more efficient and stable. This would correspond to</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta_logit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(i</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> theta_logit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span><font color=\"#000000\">i</font></span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\">x[jj[i]] * </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">...;</span></font><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span></div><div><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bernoulli_logit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_logit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(136,0,0)\"><br></span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\">With a bit of restructuring you could also use vectorization for x since almost all of them have the same normal(0,1). So if you separate the two x&#39;s that are treated differently from the others you could then just do x ~ normal(0,1), which is better than repeatedly calling normal(0,1) in a loop. <br></span></font><br>There might be other things too, but these are what I noticed right away. Hope that helps, </div><div><br></div><div>Jonah</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Sunday, October 11, 2015 at 8:27:54 PM UTC-4, Guilherme Jardim Duarte wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div><br></div>I&#39;m a newbie and I don&#39;t know if I&#39;m doing this right.<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to run a ideal points model based on &quot;legislators&quot; by Simon Jackman. This model was originally written in WinBUGS and I&#39;m coding it in Stan. </div><div><br></div><div>Unfortunately, my algorithm has got stuck here for hours:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\">&quot;<span style=\"font-size:8pt;line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\">SAMPLING FOR MODEL &#39;5d63bb8f5de6f7104af8cc8a19924b0d&#39; NOW (CHAIN 1).</span></font></span></div><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\">\r\nChain 1, Iteration:     1 / 12000 [  0%]  (Warmup)&quot;</font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\">I don&#39;t know if it is normal or I&#39;m making a mistake with my model (posted below).</font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><br></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\">Could someone check it?</font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\">Guilherme</font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font color=\"#000000\">PS: </font><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I have seen there&#39;s another post about the same algorithm (&#39;legislators&#39;) here ( <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/stan-users/OWyrW9176f8/Z_fY1t2WwM4J\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!msg/stan-users/OWyrW9176f8/Z_fY1t2WwM4J&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463492800000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hvw_MLEA_6Jeg9OnXqPrk\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/stan-users/OWyrW9176f8/Z_fY1t2WwM4J</a> ) but I decided to start a new one because I thought my issues were specific.</span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font color=\"#000000\">The complete code: &lt; <a href=\"http://github.com/duarteguilherme/legislators-based/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://github.com/duarteguilherme/legislators-based/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463492800000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NS7XwE3sRm7mpKgpgCVWp\">http://github.com/duarteguilherme/legislators-based/</a> &gt;</font></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\">My model is this:</font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">&#39;data {\r\n  int&lt;lower=0&gt; N;\r\n  int&lt;lower=0&gt; L; // legisladores\r\n  int&lt;lower=0&gt; K; // rollcalls\r\n  int&lt;lower=0&gt; jj[N];\r\n  int&lt;lower=0&gt; kk[N];\r\n  int&lt;lower=0, upper=1&gt; y[N];\r\n}\r\nparameters {\r\n  real beta0[K];\r\n  real beta1[K];\r\n  real x[L];\r\n}\r\ntransformed parameters {\r\n}\r\n\r\nmodel {\r\nfor (i in 1:N){\r\n    y[i] ~ bernoulli(Phi_approx(x[jj[i]]*beta1[kk[i]] - beta0[kk[i]]));\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\nfor (i in 1:40){ x[i] ~ normal(0,1); }\r\n  for (i in 42:65){ x[i] ~ normal(0,1); }\r\n  for (i in 67:100){ x[i] ~ normal(0,1); }\r\n  beta1 ~ normal(0, 2);\r\n  beta0 ~ normal(0, 2);\r\n  x[41] ~ normal(-1, .0001);\r\n  x[66] ~ normal(1, .0001);\r\n}\r\n&#39;</pre><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all;line-height:13px;font-size:8pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>sessionInfo()\r\n</span>R version 3.2.2 (2015-08-14)\r\nPlatform: x86_64-pc-linux-gnu (64-bit)\r\nRunning under: Debian GNU/Linux 8 (jessie)\r\n\r\nlocale:\r\n [1] LC_CTYPE=pt_BR.UTF-8       LC_NUMERIC=C               LC_TIME=pt_BR.UTF-8       \r\n [4] LC_COLLATE=pt_BR.UTF-8     LC_MONETARY=pt_BR.UTF-8    LC_MESSAGES=pt_BR.UTF-8   \r\n [7] LC_PAPER=pt_BR.UTF-8       LC_NAME=C                  LC_ADDRESS=C              \r\n[10] LC_TELEPHONE=C             LC_MEASUREMENT=pt_BR.UTF-8 LC_IDENTIFICATION=C       \r\n\r\nattached base packages:\r\n[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     \r\n\r\nloaded via a namespace (and not attached):\r\n[1] tools_3.2.2</font></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
