     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Also, the priors you&#39;re using for <font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">x[41] </font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">and</font><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> </font></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\">x[66] </span><span style=\"line-height:13px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">might be an issue. With standard deviations that small you might as well just not estimate them. </font></span></font></div>"
